@	
o	-help|-h	Show help for xxd	
o	-autoskip|-a	Toggle autoskip: A single '*' replaces nul-lines. Default off	
o	-bits|-b	Switch to bits (binary digits) dump, rather than hexdump	
o	-cols|-c	Format <cols> octets per line. Default 16	v
o	-capitalize|-C	Capitalize variable names in C include file style, when using -i	
o	-EBCDIC|-E	Change the character encoding in the righthand column from ASCII to EBCDIC	
o	-e	Switch to little-endian hexdump	
o	-groupsize|-g	Separate the output of every <bytes> bytes	v
o	-include|-i	Output in C include file style	
o	-len|-l	Stop after writing <len> octets	v
o	-name|-n	Override the variable name output when -i is used	v
o	-o	Add <offset> to the displayed file position	v
o	-postscript|-plain|-ps|-p	Output in postscript continuous hexdump style	
o	-revert|-r	Reverse operation: convert (or patch) hexdump into binary	
o	-seek	When used after -r: revert with <offset> added to file positions found in hexdump	v
o	-u	Use upper case hex letters. Default is lower case	
o	-version|-v	Show version string	
